// ======== BMP, writing ========
//
// One 24-bit BMP writer for every package that wants to save a picture: the
// 54-byte header (file header and the 40-byte information header, 2835
// pixels a meter each way), then the rows bottom first, each pixel stored
// blue, green, red, each row padded with zeros to a multiple of 4 bytes.

// The picture as a BMP file's bytes, as one buffer of a Chain (so
// 'Chain.contiguous(0, len)' lends it whole). 'pixels' is width * height
// pixels of 'channels' bytes each (3 red, green, blue; 4 adds alpha, which is
// dropped), in rows left to right; 'bottomFirst' says the first row is the
// picture's bottom (render's Image) rather than its top (a canvas, a read-back).
pub extern fn encodeBmp(width: i32, height: i32, channels: i32, pixels: &Array[u8], bottomFirst: bool) Chain;

